WEBVTT

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:10.910
There are already Ashikabi among you who stand no chance of winning, and thus are planning on dropping out.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.470
All the Sekirei in possession of these individuals shall hereby cease to function!

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.770
This period shall last for two weeks from this day on.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.810
Those who fully understand the given conditions, go and fight to your heart's content!

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.230
You...

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.470
Doing something uncalled for yet again...

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.900
Well, the North shouldn't have any problems this time.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.870
In any case, most Ashikabi are just regular people forced into this game.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:43.770
Evidently, not very many of them would try to wind up in a dangerous fight intentionally.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.230
Almost 40% of them don't even have a single win.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:05.380
atarashii yakusoku ga kokoro wo tsuyoku tsunagu

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:05.380
Our new promise binds our hearts together strongly

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:12.470
kawaru sekai ni kane ga hibiku yukou

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:12.470
The bell rings in the changing world, let's go

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:19.310
owari naki tatakai ga subete wo hiki saitemo

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:19.310
Even if the endless fight shreds everything apart,

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:25.490
kimi no hohoemi tada shinjite

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:25.490
I will believe in your smile

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.700
kimi no yume mamoreru nara

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.700
If I can protect your dream,

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.290
itami sae dakishimeyou

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.290
I will even embrace pain

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:42.590
kasane au kono omoi mune no chikai yuzurenai

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:42.590
I can't let go of these piling feelings, this oath in my heart

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:49.340
aa, sora no haruka hate made

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:49.340
Ah, all the way to the end of the sky,

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:57.560
sou, kakete yuku you na kasoku shiteku jounetsu

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.140
yes, my passion accelerates

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.560
as if it were rushing through my body

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:03.730
aa, donna unmei datte

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:03.730
Ah, no matter what kind of fate awaits me,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:14.870
sou, takaku koeteku makenai yuuki kureta kara

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:08.030
yes, I can fly high over it

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:14.870
because you gave me this undefeatable courage

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.440
Forcefully cease to function...?

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.320
So it's finally come down to this.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:37.910
Well, in your case, this rule doesn't apply because Musubi-tan already managed to beat 2 other opponents, though...

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:47.120
But there's no way I can agree with forcibly separating an Ashikabi and his Sekirei just because they lack a single win!

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.170
That's why I'm saying that you're naive!

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.050
The whole meaning behind the Sekirei's existence is to fight!

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:59.350
Sekirei who refuse to fight are unnecessary in the Sekirei Project!

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.570
Tsukiumi...

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.100
No. She's certainly got a good point.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:10.380
It would've ended up this way sooner or later, anyway.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:17.280
As long as the Sekirei Project is in a state of battle royal,
no progress will ever come unless the Ashikabi make their move.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.630
Forcing the passive Sekirei and Ashikabi to surface, huh?

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.500
He's thought it through.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.820
We've got quite a few wins ourselves.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:32.150
This matter has nothing to do with us.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.930
Have you considered the possibility that the desperate ones will come after us?

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.750
Well, wouldn't that be exciting?

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.410
This concerns us as well, doesn't it?

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:49.320
We fought in order to find some clues about Kuu-chan,

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:52.740
so we didn't need to stop their functioning...

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.990
At this rate, we both will...

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.160
Then it's settled.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.870
Shiina, we're aiming for victory from now on!

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.500
'Cause, I don't want to get separated from you...

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.700
Hey, Seo, what are we going to do?

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.840
Since Homura just kept getting away...

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:18.260
We weren't able to win any battles either.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.000
I wonder what we should do...

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:22.970
Hibiki!

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.350
What?

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.970
Do we have any beer left in the fridge?

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:27.770
Huh?

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.980
Try to be serious for once!

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.950
Hey, Master. What's that message about?

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.910
Things just keep getting more interesting...

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.630
Anyway, let's deal with our empty stomachs first.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:44.880
Let's get something to eat!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:45.830
'Kay!

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.720
Just pass on the entire content of this message to her.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.040
I understand.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:57.130
Who would have thought that even the M.B.I. would encourage her...

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.470
We sure bought a lot, eh?

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.810
Yup, and all this in just one day's worth of shopping

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.770
Say, Musubi-chan...

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:14.400
Yes?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.860
Matsu-san said that the message shouldn't concern us, but...

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.810
Is that really all right?

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:23.080
It's fine.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:27.980
One of us will always be with you whenever you step out of the Inn.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:32.040
And Matsu-san's always on the lookout with her observation satellites.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:33.530
What is it?

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.460
Well, that's not what I meant...

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.300
Matsu-san?

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.220
Mina-tan, Mina-tan, you see...

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:44.510
Actually...

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:48.120
You're being followed.

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.270
There's two of them.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.760
It's most likely an Ashikabi and a Sekirei.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.650
Don't tell me... They managed to find us already?

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.650
Wh-What should we do?

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.280
What's the matter, Minato-san?

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.490
S-Someone's following us.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.250
Following us...?

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.950
Um, who are you?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.570
A Sekirei?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:23.340
You're... the Ashikabi from the North who helped Shigi escape, right?

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.970
Wouldn't it be better for us to go out there as well?

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:32.230
Well, if they wanted to attack them, they would've done so already.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:38.650
We won't be able to figure out their objective if we panic and let Tsukiumi-tan loose, either.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:40.820
Yeah, that's true.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.120
Minato still hasn't returned, huh?

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.280
Right, Kusano?

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.680
And I suck at rock-paper-scissors, too.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:58.060
Isn't there any way to beat Musubi other than shopping and rock-paper-scissors?

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:03.970
Ashikabi of the North, I'd like to have a word with you.

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.100
A-Ashikabi of the North?

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:12.310
A few comrades of mine - including myself -
have put together a plan to escape the Capital.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:15.440
Y-You know Shigi-kun?

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:20.390
I don't really know him, but we've played around in this game for a while now, so...

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:22.040
Played around...?

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.800
That's when I met him.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:27.390
He had an absolutely weak Sekirei with him, didn't he?

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:28.780
It was just laughable.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:35.310
Well, I feel more confident now that I know even a weakling like him made it out.

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:36.290
A weakling?

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:39.660
Though, they sure left at a good time.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:44.870
If I knew this kind of message was about to come, we would've taken off ages ago.

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:46.970
So, buddy...

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.420
Won't you help us?

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:52.140
You can join us as well, if you want.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.100
Escape from the Capital...?

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.060
Musubi-chan, wake up!

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.250
Come on! Wake up, Musubi-chan!

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:04.010
I went to meet that Seo guy first, but...

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.070
Seo-san?

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.570
No way.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:10.240
You guys will die.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:13.200
And he told you about me?

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.300
What are you talking about?

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:19.640
There's no Ashikabi who hasn't heard about that incident.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:22.100
You're pretty famous, you know.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:25.550
You went against the Disciplinary Squad as well, right?

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:29.620
There's no way those weaklings could escape on their own.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.030
They're not weak.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.350
Kuno-san isn't weak at all.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:36.300
Yeah...

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.820
If Seo-san told you it's impossible, then he's right.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:45.240
Someone like you, who casually plays around and calls the determined Shigi-kun a weakling...

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:47.400
I can't help you.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:54.950
It's the M.B.I.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:57.280
This is bad. Let's go, Nanaha!

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:13.550
So the M.B.I. is already hunting them down...

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.940
Hey there, Muu-chan.

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:29.240
Karasuba-sama!

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:30.800
What are you doing here?

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.250
I'm working.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.790
You're looking quite interesting there, Muu-chan.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:36.950
Oh?

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:40.500
Your Sekirei core is shining brighter than ever.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.130
Right! I've learned the Bear Paw technique!

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:46.570
I'm looking forward to our promised day.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.590
I'll be waiting for you at the top.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:51.890
All right!

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.750
The Disciplinary Squad...

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:01.040
Minato-san,

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.820
those two are already...

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.410
I'm home.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:18.600
A lot happened, even though we just went out for a bit.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:20.460
Minato!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.170
You took too long!

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:27.970
I-I'm sorry!

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.720
So that's what it was?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:40.270
All the Ashikabi who tried to escape independently failed, so it's only natural they would try it in groups.

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:43.520
Sorry, I refused without discussing it with you-

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:44.730
Of course you did!

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:48.440
I acknowledged Kuno's case just because it was successful,

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.400
but I won't ever aid those who try to run away!

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:57.250
First they play around all they want, and once it gets dangerous they make a run for it...

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:00.120
I don't like this one bit.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:02.710
I think Minato-san's right.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:09.420
Sahashi, I think all your Sekirei feel the same way.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.590
I-I see... Thank you...

00:11:12.590 --> 00:11:15.390
Well, it was right of you to refuse.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:19.710
Talking about something like that in public was really careless.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:25.170
The fact that M.B.I. was already onto them meant that they were going to fail anyway

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:26.560
Hey, Matsu-san.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:29.570
What do you think happened to those two?

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:33.360
The Disciplinary Squad's No. 04 showing up can mean only one thing...

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:35.320
They are probably...

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.240
Yes...

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.700
I sort of understand now.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.200
So that's how it is, Yume.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:49.350
That's why you gave her your soul.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:54.050
She really might become stronger than you.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.320
It's thrilling.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:05.860
Ah! Found them!

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:09.900
The Ashikabi was taken into M.B.I.'s custody,

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:14.330
and No. 78, Nanaha, has ceased to function.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:18.550
I guess this is it for their escape plan.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:21.940
The Disciplinary Squad...

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:24.170
No. 04, Karasuba.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:27.690
There's probably no one who could stand up to her at this point.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:31.600
It would be a different story if the ex-Disciplinary Squad's No. 01 decided to make a move, though.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.060
Hey, Matsu-san.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:41.240
That No. 01 that often appears in your stories, where is she right now?

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.430
No more on that topic, Sahashi.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.900
A scary Hanya will come and eat you.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:51.070
Everyone, the dinner's served.

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.030
Oh, Landlady!

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:58.300
Oh, forgive us for not being able to help.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.220
Sahashi-san.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:00.210
Ah, yes?

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:03.210
No. 01 is already dead.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.170
Along with the M.B.I.'s Asama Takehito.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.630
L-Landlady...

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:11.760
Come. Let's go get some dinner, Minato-san.

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:17.060
Hey, Musubi! You don't have to lock arms with him!

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.830
M-Matsu didn't say a thing. No she did not.

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.100
We didn't, either.

00:13:21.890 --> 00:13:25.370
Thanks to him, I was able to meet many people,

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:29.160
I've lived my life as a person, and now I'm here.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.510
I'm already different from how I used to be.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.010
All right, the examination's all done!

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.450
You can put your clothes on.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.770
Ah, Kaoru-kun?

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:45.040
Did you do what I asked you to? The cleaning of the house I'm moving into this fall...

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.340
What? You forgot?

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.010
Kaoru-kun...

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.190
I'm sorry.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:54.270
Right. It's fine as long as you understand.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.930
Then, I'll give you a call when I head back.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:57.580
'Kay...

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:58.770
What's up with that reluctant voice?

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:02.360
That's because... You abuse people!

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:06.330
That's the first time you smiled for me.

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:10.400
Love?

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:13.520
Oh, come on, Kagari-san.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.320
Oh, this kind of stuff is so nice.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.250
I really loved him.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.750
To the point that I would forget my own purpose.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:23.600
Miya-tan...

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:27.860
But these thoughts eventually...

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:31.170
led to his death.

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:35.840
How's that? I win!

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:38.220
Tsukiumi-tan, you broke the rules.

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:39.510
Wh-What?!

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:41.900
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:45.150
You have to say Uno when you win!

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:47.990
U-Uno!

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:50.940
Too late for that now.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:53.070
C'mon, let it slide!

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.930
The rules are the rules.

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:55.770
The rules!

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.690
Wh-Why you...

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.030
Uno!

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:00.540
What the-!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.000
Oh, my! Kuu-chan wins again?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.790
Kuu-chan, you're amazing!

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:06.670
Why?!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.950
Really?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:09.520
My, isn't it lively in here?

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.130
Sorry for bothering you, Landlady.

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:14.030
What are you guys doing?

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:16.260
U-Um...

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:22.920
Kusano, as the next legal wife, has decided upon this as another challenge following shopping and rock-paper-scissors...

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.270
But why the hell is Kusano first?!

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:30.670
So that's it.

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:33.900
You're quite popular as usual, Sahashi-san.

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:35.860
L-Landlady...

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:40.510
But if you were to try doing something lecherous here...

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:42.820
I won't!

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:45.330
I'd never even think of doing something like that!

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.010
Good night.

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:52.420
Uno!

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:54.590
Kuu-chan wins again!

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:57.010
Why can't I win at all?!

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:03.970
This game is heavily based on luck, so it's difficult even with my genius brain...

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:06.890
Kusano-tan, where did you learn to play like this?

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:09.880
I used to play a lot with U-chan.

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.040
With Uzume?

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:11.860
Yeah!

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:16.740
Here, arrange your hand like this and tease the others by slowing down the game.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:19.550
The simple ones will fall for it.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:24.230
The simple one, huh?

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.990
Wh-What are you guys implying?!

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:32.380
I'd like to play with U-chan too.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:39.430
Oh, I just got a great idea!

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:45.100
How about this: whoever wins gets to go on a date with Minato-kun tomorrow.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:49.780
Hold on, Kazehana-san! I didn't agree to that!

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:52.130
Then, how about the loser strips?

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:54.020
How's that?

00:16:57.890 --> 00:16:59.870
A date is fine!

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:02.120
Come on, the Landlady will kill me!

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:08.040
In that case, I'm going to win and show you an adult's day out.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:11.210
I can't lose this one!

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:13.380
I won't lose, either!

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:16.300
Time to get serious for once!

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.940
I get, I get...

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:23.720
I get that the victim's opinion won't be considered at all...

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:24.390
Huh?

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:26.120
Kagari-san?

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:31.200
Uzume...

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.440
Chiho, look!

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.620
It's a beautiful full moon.

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:39.400
It really is. It's so round and pretty.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.820
I wish the two of us could fly all the way there.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:44.320
You're right.

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:48.220
Forgetting everything and just flying away.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.950
We're off!

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:54.920
I'm off...

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.430
Be careful!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:01.430
Listen up! This date is limited to 4 hours!

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:03.880
You're dead if it takes even a minute longer!

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:04.890
O-Okay...

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.850
Okay!

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:11.940
What a terrible hangover...

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:16.050
You sure drank a lot during the game yesterday.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.740
What do you mean?

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:22.030
But that was a nice move last night, Kazehana-tan.

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:28.390
Things could've gotten difficult if Mina-tan kept having Uzume-tan on his mind.

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:34.970
All the Sekirei defeated by the Clothed Sekirei were classified with "Winner Unknown."

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:39.960
Which means that Uzume-tan's win count is zero.

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:44.130
So she might show up as our enemy next time.

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:45.590
That's right...

00:18:45.590 --> 00:18:47.050
That's certainly possible.

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:51.870
Once Mina-tan realizes that as well, he probably will...

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:56.980
It's been a long time since I've been out.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:00.980
The doctor said you're free to go outside since you're feeling so well today.

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:05.950
You almost forget that the sky is so vast from behind that window.

00:19:06.470 --> 00:19:12.830
Not just the sky; the wide open ocean and high mountains as well. Let's go see them together sometime.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.870
I wonder if I can do that.

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:17.450
You can. Definitely.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.970
The wind's picking up, so I'll fetch you a blanket.

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:23.670
Just wait a second.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.670
Wind?

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:26.570
Uzume-chan.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:30.870
You'll stay with me forever, right?

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.270
What are you saying? Of course I will!

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.790
I'll always be with you.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.230
Jeez.

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:45.030
I'll have to steal one from your lips if you say something weird like that again.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.770
Oh, Uzume-chan...

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:49.920
Wait for me here. I'll be back in a moment.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:50.410
Okay.

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:55.750
Did you have fun?

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:59.530
Yup! Kuu had so much fun!

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:02.210
Thanks, Onii-chan! I love you!

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:07.610
We just went shopping at the department store and had a bite to eat...

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:10.910
Kuu-chan?

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.310
Functions stopped?

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:18.270
We came to tell you since your Ashikabi is unable to use a cell phone.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:21.490
How nice of you.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.480
I have no reason to tell you this,

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:23.910
but you're-

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.190
I know already.

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:29.540
There's no way anyone's keeping a win record of this dirty job.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:33.870
But you can't just sit back and have them disable you, can you?

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:38.160
For the sake of your beloved Ashikabi, too.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:39.000
Right?

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:46.050
And that is why Higa-sama has decided to provide you with a chance to win.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:51.580
But your only choice is the Ashikabi in the Northern area, he said.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:52.550
In the Northern area...?

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:57.980
However, this is not an order.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:01.560
Whether you do it or not is up to you.

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:02.390
I'll do it.

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:04.200
Very well.

00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:06.860
Kuu-chan!

00:21:07.060 --> 00:21:08.280
Kuu-chan!

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:11.700
Where did she go?

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.660
The hospital?

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:19.310
How cute!

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:20.500
Kitty-cat!

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:22.210
Kitty-cat!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:26.590
Hello.

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:28.670
Hello.

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:36.520
It makes no difference if I can protect Chiho's life.

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:41.930
Even if the ones I have to defeat are my precious friends...

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:44.110
No matter who it is...

